province = 70
blurb = "Depicts village women carrying kindling, tools and a ladder. The location is yase village in Kyōto, still standing at the foot of Mount Hiei today.

The women are [url=https://www.japan-experience.com/all-about-japan/kyoto/temples-shrines/oharame-the-peddler-maidens-of-ohara-kyoto]\"ōharame\"[/url], female peddlers of kindling from the nearby village of Ōhara. They had elaborate hairstyles around which they wrapped towels, placing the kindling on top of it to make the trek to Kyōto. They blackened their teeth and wore tight-sleeved kimonos with white leggings underneath.

Tourists today can visit the village's visitor center to dress up as ōharame, and there's an annual Ōharame Festival as well."
